From 7c663cbfc8e6050b9345d28fd3f0cc35a089d195 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild-Idler Patch Tool <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:46:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0227: Replayable Quest Chains -- resolution logic and
 purchasing

Step (3) of the sequencing plan. Renumbered from an originally-
generated 0226 -- that number landed first from a parallel thread's
unrelated Vendor Rep/Grimsby's Tab patch, same collision shape as the
earlier 0189 incident. Reconciled the three files both patches
touched (guild-idler-status.md, tuning.json, engine.ts); types.ts,
GuildManager.ts, QuestManager.ts applied with zero overlap.

Wires the data model (0224) and loot mechanism (0225) into something
a hero can actually be sent on. Still no dedicated UI.

QuestManager.chainReplayOffer: replay counterpart to chainOffer, with
the chosen difficulty's successPenalty/durationMultiplier baked into
baseSuccess/duration at generation time.

New fields, not overloading existing ones: QuestOffer.chain.replay,
QuestResult.chainReplayAdvanced.

QuestManager.resolve's chain section now branches three ways:
ordinary quest (untouched), first-clear chain stage (untouched), or
replay (new). Replay branch: padding loot tagged
chainReplayHeroic/chainReplayLegendary; dedicated item chance roll on
a completed final stage (baseDropChance + difficulty's lootBonus,
never at Normal); full attempt reset to stage 0 on failure; never
touches ChainDef's own first-clear-only rewards.

GuildManager.buyChainReplayTier: flat one-time gold, no levels.

Two new engine actions: startChainReplay(heroId, chainId, difficulty),
buyChainReplayTier(tierId).

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and npx vite build both pass clean against
the reconciled tree (both this patch's and the Vendor Rep patch's
changes together). Every Tuning.get() call actually verified by
script against registered ids -- 18/18 match. No duplicate Tuning ids.
